Wrote `coder-3.json` with one row for `transportation-priorities`. SB 960 is Wiener's own authored/signed bill (`own-act`, `record`), but its operative clauses only require adding complete-streets (bike/ped/transit) elements into existing SHOPP highway-maintenance planning — it never sets or compares investment levels for new road capacity, so it can't separate rungs 1–3. Coded `direction-only`, row BLANK.
